vables disappeared from DOM but sections data remained. When shown again, preview fully restored with all content intact: John Test Smith contact info, summary text, StartupXYZ experience, MIT education, section order preserved, custom \\\"My Contact Details\\\" title retained. Template (Minimal) unchanged.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-6\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Duplicated \\\"Software Engineer Resume\\\" → new resume \\\"Software Engineer Resume (Copy)\\\" created with all original content (Alex Morgan contact, summary, 2 experience entries, 1 education entry, 5 skills). Renamed copy to \\\"Financial Analyst Resume\\\" successfully. Edited copy's name to \\\"Jordan Smith\\\". Verified original still shows \\\"Alex Morgan\\\" unchanged. Duplicate is fully independent.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-7\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Current session shows 5 distinct resume variations on dashboard: (1) Financial Analyst Resume (Modern, Aug 25 2026), (2) Untitled Resume (Minimal, Aug 25 2026 - created with full content), (3) Product Designer Resume (Minimal, Feb 25 2024), (4) Marketing Manager Resume (Classic, Feb 10 2024), (5) Software Engineer Resume (Modern, Jan 20 2024). Each is accessible and independently editable with distinct content and templates.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-8\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Search tested: typed \\\"financial\\\" (lowercase) → found \\\"Financial Analyst Resume\\\" (case-insensitive). Cleared search field → all 5 resumes restored. Sort tested: (1) \\\"Newest First\\\" shows Aug 25, 2026 resumes at top (2) Changed to \\\"Oldest First\\\" → Software Engineer Resume (Jan 20, 2024) moved to top (3) Changed back to \\\"Newest First\\\" → correct order restored.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-19\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Date filter not implemented\", \"actual\": \"No date filter UI controls found on dashboard. Dashboard shows: (1) Search input (text-based filtering), (2) Sort dropdown (Newest/Oldest/Title A-Z/Z-A), (3) Resume cards showing \\\"Updated [date]\\\" text. No input fields or controls for filtering by exact date or date range exist. Semantic hints show only: dashboard.create, dashboard.search, dashboard.sort, dashboard.resumes - no date-related controls.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-9\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"No date validation - invalid dates accepted without error\", \"actual\": \"Tested with experience entry: (1) Changed end date from 2026-08 to 2023-12 (before start date 2024-01) - accepted silently, preview shows \\\"Jan 2024 Dec 2023\\\". (2) Changed end date to 2027-12 (future date, today is Aug 25, 2026) - accepted silently, preview shows \\\"Jan 2024 Dec 2027\\\". No error messages, validation dialogs, or feedback provided for either invalid scenario. Invalid dates persist in the resume.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-10\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Date format is consistent: \\\"Jan 2024\\\" (abbreviated month + Year). Tested \\\"I currently work here\\\" toggle: (1) When unchecked - end date field enabled with value \\\"2026-08\\\". (2) When checked - end date field cleared (value=\\\"\\\"), disabled (enabled=false), and preview updated from \\\"Jan 2024 Aug 2026\\\" to \\\"Jan 2024 Present\\\". Education dates also show consistent format: \\\"Sep 2015 Jun 2019\\\".\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-11\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Resume changes not persisted across page reload\", \"actual\": \"Created and edited \\\"Untitled Resume\\\" (with contact info, summary, experience, education, skills, changed template to Minimal) and duplicated/renamed to \\\"Financial Analyst Resume\\\" during session. Before reload, dashboard showed 5 resumes (3 original + 2 new). After reload, only 3 original resumes remain (Product Designer, Marketing Manager, Software Engineer). Untitled Resume and Financial Analyst Resume completely disappeared. No persistence of session changes.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-21\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Empty title validation not implemented\", \"actual\": \"Opened rename dialog for \\\"Software Engineer Resume\\\", cleared the title field to empty string, clicked Save. The empty title was accepted and saved. Resume now displays with empty name (\\\"\\\") on dashboard. No validation error or feedback provided. No mechanism to reject empty/whitespace-only titles. Current title was overwritten with empty string instead of being preserved.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-12\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Changed contact full name from \\\"Sarah Chen\\\" to \\\"Sarah Johnson\\\". Preview updated immediately (preview.contact.name changed to \\\"Sarah Johnson\\\") without any manual save button or refresh. No delay observed between field input and preview update.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-13\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Hid Skills section by clicking visibility toggle. Preview updated immediately - \\\"SKILLS\\\" heading and skills text disappeared from preview without page refresh. Section visibility toggle showed visible.value=false. Layout change reflected in real-time.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-14\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Changed name from \\\"Sarah Chen\\\" to \\\"Sarah Johnson\\\" and hid Skills section. Clicked back to dashboard - resume showed \\\"Updated Aug 25, 2026\\\" (timestamp changed from Feb 10, 2024). Reopened resume - name change retained (\\\"Sarah Johnson\\\"), Skills section still hidden. Auto-save confirmed without manual save button.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-15\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Current resume shows all visible sections in preview: Contact (name, email, phone, location, LinkedIn), Professional Summary, Work Experience (2 entries), Education (2 entries). Skills section hidden (not rendered). All visible sections with content are shown. Preview is readable - no truncation or missing content observed. Scrollable collection lists display all items.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-16\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Tested in current session: (1) Navigated from Contact tab → Sections tab → back to Contact tab. Name \\\"Sarah Johnson\\\" retained. (2) Went to dashboard and reopened resume. All content intact: name, email, phone, location, LinkedIn, summary text, 2 experience entries, 2 education entries. (3) Section visibility change (Skills hidden) persisted. Content retained across all navigation scenarios within session.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-17\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Tested in FT-6: Duplicated \\\\\\\"Software Engineer Resume\\\\\\\" (original with Alex Morgan, 2 experience entries, 1 education, 5 skills). Copy auto-named \\\\\\\"Software Engineer Resume (Copy)\\\\\\\" with identical content. Renamed copy to \\\\\\\"Financial Analyst Resume\\\\\\\". Edited copy's contact name to \\\\\\\"Jordan Smith\\\\\\\". Verified original \\\\\\\"Software Engineer Resume\\\\\\\" still displayed \\\\\\\"Alex Morgan\\\\\\\" unchanged. Duplicate editing does not affect original.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-18\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Changed resume title from \\\"Marketing Manager Resume\\\" to \\\"Senior Marketing Manager 2026\\\" in editor title input. Navigated to dashboard - resume card shows new title \\\"Senior Marketing Manager 2026\\\". New title appears in both editor and dashboard. Title change persisted across navigation.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-20\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Changed Experience section heading from \\\"Experience\\\" to \\\"Professional Experience\\\". Preview updated immediately to show \\\"PROFESSIONAL EXPERIENCE\\\" (in uppercase as per Minimal template styling). Custom heading text displayed in preview. Also verified that Summary section already had custom title \\\"About Me\\\" showing in preview. Custom section headings are rendered with customized text in the resume preview.\"}]}"
